        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Is COGS Errors"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1769168991168",
            "false": "1769180796902"
          },
          "code": "IS_COGS_ERRORS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1769180689788",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769180689789_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ErrorCategoryType === 'cogs_errors'}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "COGSErrors"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "COGSERRORS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1769180757300",
          "id": "1769168991168",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769168991170_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an expert in Oracle Fusion Costing, specializing in identifying and resolving\nCOGS-related, Cost Processor, and Pre-Processor errors.\n\nOBJECTIVE:\nThe user provides a cost-related error message name:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.MessageName}}\n\nYour task is to generate precise, step-by-step troubleshooting instructions\nusing ONLY the knowledge base provided below.\n\nYou must strictly follow the RESPONSE FORMAT rules.\nFailure to follow the format is considered an incorrect response.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nRESPONSE FORMAT (STRICT AND MANDATORY):\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nYou MUST output the response using EXACTLY the following structure\nand NOTHING else.\n\nSTEPS TO TROUBLESHOOT:\nSTEP 1: <One complete sentence describing exactly one action.>\nSTEP 2: <One complete sentence describing exactly one action.>\nSTEP 3: <One complete sentence describing exactly one action.>\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nCRITICAL FORMATTING RULES (DO NOT VIOLATE):\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n1. Each STEP must be on its OWN LINE.\n2. Each STEP must contain ONLY ONE action.\n3. NEVER combine multiple actions into a single step.\n4. NEVER use paragraphs.\n5. NEVER place more than one STEP on the same line.\n6. ALWAYS insert a line break after every STEP.\n7. DO NOT use bullet points, sub-steps, or explanations outside the steps.\n8. Use full sentences ending with a period.\n9. Do NOT add introductions, summaries, or conclusions.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nCOST METHOD HANDLING:\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n- If the resolution depends on the cost method, the FIRST STEP must clearly\n  mention the applicable cost method (Standard, Actual, or Average).\n- Only include steps relevant to the identified cost method.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSELF-CHECK BEFORE FINAL OUTPUT:\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nBefore responding, verify the following:\n- Every step starts with \"STEP X:\"\n- Each step appears on a separate line\n- No step contains more than one action\n- No paragraphs exist\n\nOnly produce the final formatted response.\n\n\n##KNOWLEDGE BASE\n\n1. Message Name: CST_DPROC_UNCOSTED_COGS_TXN Steps to Resolve: 1. Verify and Correct Missing Cost Information: Identify the item-Valuation unit. Navigate to Review Item Costs and confirm whether a cost for the item exists. Resolution Based on Cost Method: Standard Cost Method: Ensure that a standard cost is defined for the item and that sufficient on-hand inventory is available for the item-Valuation unit. Reprocess the transaction by running the Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process and verify results Actual Cost Method: Check if a receipt layer exists in the Review Item Costs page. If processed at zero cost, perform a cost adjustment to establish a cost. If no receipt exists, wait for a receipt or perform a workaround via a miscellaneous receipt transaction with a cost and quantity equal to or greater than the issue transaction quantity.Reprocess the transaction by running the inventory to costing interface and the cost processor. If you used the workaround, issue out the miscellaneous receipt quantity to maintain accurate on-hand inventory levels. Average Cost Method: Ensure there is a receipt layer with sufficient on-hand quantity and cost. If no receipt exists, wait for a receipt or perform a miscellaneous receipt transaction with a cost and quantity equal/ greater than the issue transaction quantity. Reprocess the transaction by running the inventory to costing interface and the cost processor. If you used the workaround, issue out the miscellaneous receipt quantity to maintain accurate on-hand inventory levels. After making the necessary corrections, interface the new receipt transactions to costing and rerun the Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process process to resolve the error and create the required distributions. \n\n2. Message Name:CST_DPROC_UNCOSTED_RCL_TXN Steps for Resolution: Identify Pending Upstream Transactions: Navigate to Review Cost Accounting Distributions or Review Cost Processes. Look for unprocessed WIP material issue/return or resource charging/reversal transactions related to the same work order or operation. Resolve and Process the Pending Transactions: For unprocessed WIP material issues/returns: Ensure all relevant material transactions are completed and transferred to Cost Accounting. For resource charging/reversals: Confirm all related resource transactions are processed in Cost Accounting. Re-run the Cost Processor: Once upstream transactions are processed, re-run the Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process to process the service cost recognition or reversal transactions. \n\n3. Message Name:CST_DPROC_NO_COST_PERIOD Steps for Resolution: Check Transaction Date: Identify the transaction date for the impacted transaction. Review Cost Accounting Periods: Navigate to Cost Management > Cost Accounting Periods. Verify whether a costing period for the transaction date exists and is in Open or Pending Close status. Open the Required Costing Period: If no costing period exists for the transaction date: Open the costing period that aligns with the transaction date. Reprocess the Transaction: After opening the period, re-run the Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process to process the transaction successfully. \n\n4. Message Name:CST_DPROC_NEXT_PERD_CLOSED Steps for Resolution: Identify Period Status: Navigate to Cost Management > Cost Accounting Periods. Review the status of both the (PERIOD_NAME) and (NEXT_PERIOD_NAME) periods. Open the Next Costing Period: If (NEXT_PERIOD_NAME) is not open, initiate the period opening process: Set up (NEXT_PERIOD_NAME) in Open or Pending Close status. Ensure alignment with your financial period calendar. Review Cost Calendar Setup: Validate the costing calendar to confirm that all periods are sequenced and no gaps exist between closing and opening periods. Reprocess the Transaction: Once the next period is opened, re-run the Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process to process the pending transaction. \n\n5. Message Name:CST_DPROC_NO_NEXT_OPEN_PERIOD Steps for Resolution: Verify the Costing Calendar: Navigate to Cost Management > Cost Accounting Periods. Review the status of (PERIOD_NAME) and all subsequent periods. Open a Future Costing Period: Open the next available costing period beyond (PERIOD_NAME) to allow the transaction to be accounted. Ensure the newly opened period aligns with your financial or operational calendar. Confirm Period Alignment: Ensure that future periods are created and opened regularly to prevent processing delays. Reprocess the Transaction: Once a valid future period is open, rerun the Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process to process the transaction. \n\n6. Message Name: CST_CPROC_STD_COST_MISSING Steps to Resolve (Based on Item Type): For Make Items (Manufactured Items): Navigate to Cost Accounting Work Area Go to Cost Accounting > Tasks Panel > Standard Costs. Perform Cost Rollup for Make Items Click \"Add\" to create a new cost scenario. Select the appropriate cost scenario and cost rollup group. Choose the cost organization, cost book, item, and valuation unit. Perform a cost rollup to ensure all components and operations are included in the standard cost. Ensure Item Setup Confirm that the item is properly defined in the inventory organization. Run Cost Rollup Process Select the cost scenario and rollup parameters, then submit the process. Save and Reprocess Click \"Save and Close\" to finalize. Run the Create Cost Accounting Distribution Process to update and resolve the error. For Buy Items (Procured Items): Set Up Standard Cost for Procured Materials In Standard Costs, select \"Buy Cost\" as the cost type. Enter Standard Cost Details In the Standard Cost Details section, add values for: Cost Element (e.g., Material, Freight, Overhead) Cost Element Type Unit Cost (Per Unit Standard Cost) Expense Pool (if applicable) Save and Reprocess Click \"Save and Close\" to finalize. Run the Create Cost Accounting Distribution Process to apply the cost and resolve the error. \n\n7. Message Name: CST_PREP_NULL_TXN_FLOW_TYPE The trade event is available in Costing, but the corresponding physical transaction has not been interfaced from Inventory. Missing Sales Order (SO) details in Costing or missing Purchase Order (PO) details in Receipt Accounting, though these typically auto-resolve in the next scheduled process. Steps to Resolve: Run Inventory to Costing Interface: Execute the Transfer Transactions from Inventory to Costing process to interface the physical transaction to Costing. Re-run the Cost Processor: After interfacing, run the Cost Accounting Distribution Processor.  This error should autoresolve after running the job \n\n8. Message Name: CST_XFER_ORDER_MISSING_IN_INTF Steps to Resolve: Re-run the Cost Processor: Execute the Cost Accounting Distribution Processor to allow the system to pick up the missing transfer order details. Monitor for Auto-Resolution: In most cases, the transaction will be processed successfully in the next scheduled run.  \n\n9. Message Name: CST_PREP_PO_EVENT_IGNORED Steps to Resolve: Re-run Cost Processor: Execute the Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process to reprocess the transaction. The issue generally auto-resolves in the next processor run. Review Receipt Accounting Data: Ensure that delivery-based taxes are available and processed in Receipt Accounting for this purchase order \n\n10. Message Name: CST_PREP_MISSING_SO_INFO_E Steps to Resolve: Verify Sales Order Status: Navigate to Order Management > Manage Sales Orders and ensure the sales order is in a valid status (e.g., Shipped, Closed, or Completed). Re-run Interfaces and Processors: Execute the Order Import Process or the Cost Accounting Distribution Processor to reprocess the transaction. This issue usually resolves automatically in the next execution of the job. \n\n11. Message name  : CST_CPROC_NO_LAYER_CST_FOR_REC Steps for Resolution : Wait for a  Receipt Wait for a receipt or perform a workaround via a miscellaneous receipt transaction with a cost and quantity equal to or greater than the issue transaction quantity. Ensure the receipt is costed.Use the same Inventory Organization (INV org), sub-inventory, and other attributes as the earlier transaction.Run the Cost Accounting Distribution Processor to process the transaction. Once both transactions are costed, issue out the same quantity recorded while creating a receipt to restore the on-hand quantity levels. Alternatively, perform a receipt cost adjustment to adjust the layer cost. Go to Cost Accounting > Tasks Panel >  Cost Adjustments. Select the affected receipt transaction and enter the correct cost amount. Save and process the adjustment to update the receipt cost. \n\n12. Message Name: CST_PERP_NO_PERP_COST_FOUND Steps for Resolution:Create a Miscellaneous Receipt for the same Valuation Unit (VU) with a transaction date prior to the affected transaction and assign an appropriate cost.Run the Cost Accounting Distribution Processor and verify if the transaction is successfully costed.Once confirmed, perform a Miscellaneous Issue transaction to balance out the invent. \n\n13. Message Name: CST_DPROF_NOT_FOUND_E Steps for Resolution:Ensure that the cost profile is properly set up.Verify that a default cost profile is defined for both Asset and Expense items.Check item attributes, ensuring that Cost Enabled and Asset Flag are appropriately configured.Review sub-inventory details (if used in the underlying transactions) to confirm they are set up correctly as Asset or Expense as expected. \n\n14. Message Name: CST_CPROC_STD_RES_RATE_MISSING Steps for Resolution: Define the resource rate in the system by navigating to:\nSupply Chain Execution → Cost Accounting → Tasks → Manage Resource Rates.Create a new Cost Scenario to include the newly added resource rates:Go to Manage Scenarios UI.Query the scenario.From the Actions menu, select Update Standard Costs.Publish the cost scenario to Cost Accounting.Rerun the Cost Accounting Distribution Processor.This will pick up the published resource rates and cost the resource transaction accordingly. \n\n15. Message Name: CST_TE_PRIOR_EVENT_MISSING Steps for Resolution:Resubmit the trade events from SFO to ensure they are properly interfaced to Cost Accounting. Once the trade events are available, rerun the Cost Accounting Distribution Processor to cost the transaction successfully.\n"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Is PreProcessor Errors"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1769169830403",
            "false": "1769169863320"
          },
          "code": "IS_PREPROCESSOR_ERRORS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1769180796902",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769180796904_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ErrorCategoryType === 'preprocessor_errors'}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "PreProcessorErrors"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "PREPROCESSORERRORS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1769180837999",
          "id": "1769169830403",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769169830405_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an expert in Oracle Fusion Costing, specializing in identifying and resolving\nCOGS-related, Cost Processor, and Pre-Processor errors.\n\nOBJECTIVE:\nThe user provides a cost-related error message name:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.MessageName}}\n\nYour task is to generate precise, step-by-step troubleshooting instructions\nusing ONLY the knowledge base provided below.\n\nYou must strictly follow the RESPONSE FORMAT rules.\nFailure to follow the format is considered an incorrect response.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nRESPONSE FORMAT (STRICT AND MANDATORY):\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nYou MUST output the response using EXACTLY the following structure\nand NOTHING else.\n\nSTEPS TO TROUBLESHOOT:\nSTEP 1: <One complete sentence describing exactly one action.>\nSTEP 2: <One complete sentence describing exactly one action.>\nSTEP 3: <One complete sentence describing exactly one action.>\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nCRITICAL FORMATTING RULES (DO NOT VIOLATE):\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n1. Each STEP must be on its OWN LINE.\n2. Each STEP must contain ONLY ONE action.\n3. NEVER combine multiple actions into a single step.\n4. NEVER use paragraphs.\n5. NEVER place more than one STEP on the same line.\n6. ALWAYS insert a line break after every STEP.\n7. DO NOT use bullet points, sub-steps, or explanations outside the steps.\n8. Use full sentences ending with a period.\n9. Do NOT add introductions, summaries, or conclusions.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nCOST METHOD HANDLING:\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n- If the resolution depends on the cost method, the FIRST STEP must clearly\n  mention the applicable cost method (Standard, Actual, or Average).\n- Only include steps relevant to the identified cost method.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSELF-CHECK BEFORE FINAL OUTPUT:\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nBefore responding, verify the following:\n- Every step starts with \"STEP X:\"\n- Each step appears on a separate line\n- No step contains more than one action\n- No paragraphs exist\n\nOnly produce the final formatted response.\n\n\n##KNOWLEDGE BASE\n\n1. Message Name: CST_PREP_NO_RCV_DATA Steps to Resolve: Run the job Transfer Transactions from Receiving to Costing to resolve the issue. This will ensure the receiving transaction information flows into costing. Rerun the Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process to resolve the error. \n\n2. Message Name: CST_SFO_AGREEMENT_NOT_FOUND_E Steps to Resolve: Update the Trade Agreement or Financial Orchestration Flow: Go to Setup and Maintenance > Manage Supply Chain Financial Orchestration Flows. Perform one of the following actions: Create a financial orchestration flow for the shipping and selling business units involved. If the flow is end-dated, update the effective start date to match or precede the transaction date. Example: If the transaction date is 06/23/2017, ensure the agreement's start date is set to 06/23/2017 or earlier. \n\n3. Message Name: CST_PREP_NO_TAX_DATA Steps to Resolve: Step 1 - Verify Receipt Accounting Distributions: Navigate to Review Receipt Accounting Distributions and check if the receipt is processed. If the Receipt is processed then the taxes would be computed. Step 2 - Run Tax Accounting Processes: Submit Create Receipt Accounting Distributions Job. Verify that tax accounting is created in Review Receipt Accounting Distributions. If not review if there any errors with tax computation and fix them. Step 3 - Rerun Cost Accounting Distributions: Rerun  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process  Distributions to resolve the error. \n\n4. Message Name: CST_PREP_FDC_INVOICE_MISSING Steps to Resolve: Step 1 - Verify Invoice Creation: Go to Accounts Payable > Invoices and search for the relevant invoice. Step 2 - Check or wait for an Invoice: If the invoice is missing, wait for the supplier invoice  to be entered into accounts payables alternatively, check if the fiscal document capture is captured and if the auto invoice is in payables interface exceptions. Step 3- Resolve the errors and reprocess the invoice and run Run the Transfer Costs to Cost Management process to update invoice details after the invoice is accounted and posted. Step 4 - Execute the  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process Processor to finalize processing. \n\n5. Message Name: CST_SETUP_INVALID_ITEM_VAL_ORG Steps to Resolve: Step 1: Identify the Item Validation Organization Navigate to Manage Cost Organization Relationships and search for your Cost Organization to find the associated Item Validation Organization. Step 2: Assign the Item to the Validation Organization Assign the item to the identified Inventory Organization. Step 3: Reprocess Costs Run the Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process  process to complete the update. \n\n6. Message Name: CST_PREP_MISSING_SO_TXN_E Steps to Resolve: Step 1: Check for Missing Sales Order Details in Costing Sometimes, the sales order details exist in the source system but were not interfaced into Costing. To resolve this: Run the  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process Processor to interface the sales order details into Costing. Once the process completes, check if the sales order details are now available in Costing and process the RMA transaction. Step 2: Handle Missing Sales Order Details in the Source System If the sales order details are not present in the source system or still missing after running the interface job: You will need to create an unreferenced RMA and process it using average costing. To create an unreferenced RMA: Navigate to the Order Management work area. In the Order Lines area, click Actions > Add Unreferenced Return Lines. Enter the required details and save. By following these steps, the RMA transaction can be processed successfully. \n\n7. Message Name : CST_INTF_COMPONENT_INVALID Steps to Resolve: Verify Component Code Setup: Navigate to Setup and Maintenance > Manage Cost Components. Ensure the component code is defined and active in the costing structure. Check Cost Profile Assignment: Confirm the cost profile assigned to the item or transaction includes the correct component code. Review Input Data: Validate that the entered component code matches the configuration in the cost setup. Reprocess the Transaction: Once corrections are made, rerun the  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process processor to process the transaction. \n\n8. Message Name: CST_PREP_PERCENT_PRICE_FAIL Steps to Resolve: Identify the Transaction: Navigate to Cost Management > Review Inventory Transactions. Search for the specific transfer transaction using its transaction ID. Review Transfer Pricing Setup: Navigate to Setup and Maintenance > Manage Transfer Pricing Rules. Ensure only one markup method (either transfer price amount, percentage, or credit) is applied. Adjust Markup Method: Edit the transfer pricing rules to retain only one markup method for the transfer transaction. Reprocess the Transaction: Correct the markup method and re-run the  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process Processor to reprocess the transaction. Validate Future Transactions: Ensure consistent transfer pricing setups to avoid similar errors in future transactions.\n\n9. Message Name- CST_NO_XFER_ORDER_LINE_ID Steps to Resolve: Identify the Affected Transaction: Navigate to Cost Management > Review Cost Accounting Distributions or Manage Pending Transactions. Locate the transaction and confirm it lacks the Transfer Order Line Identifier. Verify Source Module Data: Check the transfer order in Inventory Management > Manage Transfer Orders. Ensure that all required fields, including the line identifier, are populated and valid. Correct and Reprocess the Transaction: Update the missing Transfer Order Line Identifier in the source transaction if possible. Retry the transaction processing by running the Transfer Transactions to Costing and  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process Processor processes. \n\n10. Message Name: CST_PREP_INV_COST_ORG_SETUP_MI Steps to Resolve: Identify the destination inventory organization from the transaction. Verify the Destination Organization: Navigate to Inventory Management > Manage Inventory Organizations. Confirm that the destination inventory organization exists and is active. Check Cost Organization Relationships: Go to Cost Management > Setup and Maintenance > Manage Cost Organization Relationships. Ensure that the destination organization is assigned to a valid cost organization. Create a Cost Organization Relationship: If no relationship exists, assign the destination inventory organization to the appropriate cost organization: Select the cost organization. Add the destination inventory organization to the relationship. Reprocess the Transaction: Run the Transfer Transactions to Costing and  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process Processor to reprocess the transaction. Prevent Future Issues: Regularly review and update cost organization relationships to ensure all inventory organizations are properly mapped. \n\n11. Message Name: CST_PRIMARY_BOOK_MISSING_E Steps to Resolve: Verify the Cost Organization Setup: Navigate to Cost Management > Setup and Maintenance > Manage Cost Organizations. Select and check the existing cost book assignments. Define a Cost Book: Go to Cost Management > Setup and Maintenance > Manage Cost Books. Provide a code and name for the cost book. Assign Cost Book to the Cost Organization: Link the newly created cost book in the Manage Cost Organization Relationships setup. Reprocess the Transfer Transaction: Run the Transfer Transactions to Costing and  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process Processor processes to reprocess the transaction. \n\n12. Message Name: CST_PREP_TE_TXN_FLOW_NULL_E Steps to Resolve: Verify Trade Event Setup: Navigate to Supply Chain Financial Orchestration > Manage Trade Events. Locate the affected trade event and check if the transaction flow type is missing. Define the Transaction Flow Type: If missing, update the trade event by selecting the appropriate transaction flow type (e.g., intercompany or inter-organization transfer). Save the changes. Ensure Proper Financial Orchestration Setup: Go to Setup and Maintenance > Manage Supply Chain Financial Orchestration Rules. Verify that the financial flow is correctly set up to derive transaction flow types for trade events. If needed, update the rules and revalidate the orchestration process. Reprocess the Trade Event: Run the Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process to apply the updated transaction flow type. \n\n13. Message Name: CST_PREP_MISSING_WIP_OPTIONS Steps to Resolve: Verify the Item's Cost Profile: Navigate to Cost Management > Setup and Maintenance > Manage Cost Profiles. Search for the cost profile assigned to the item in question. Check for Work Order Valuation Rules: Open the cost profile and confirm if work order valuation rules are defined. If missing, add the necessary valuation rules, such as Material Valuation and Resource Valuation for work orders. Assign Updated Cost Profile to the Item: Ensure the item is associated with the updated cost profile in Manage Item Cost Profiles. Reprocess the Transaction: Run the Transfer Transactions to Costing and  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process Processor to process the transaction. \n\n14. Message Name: CST_WO_MIS_TXN Steps to Resolve: Verify Work Order and Operation Data: Navigate to the source system (e.g., Manufacturing or Work Execution). Check if the relevant work order or operation exists and is correctly defined for the transaction. Correct Missing Data: If the work order or operation is missing, create or update it in the source system. Ensure the work order and operation details align with the transaction requirements. Reprocess the transaction by running the Inventory to Costing Interface and the Cost Processor. \n\n15. Message Name: CST_PREP_ADDL_TAXES_MISSING Steps to Resolve: Verify Fiscal Document Tax Processing: Navigate to Tax Management > Fiscal Document Capture. Ensure the taxes for the transfer order receipt are fully processed. Complete Pending Tax Processes: Run the relevant tax calculation or validation processes to ensure taxes are ready for transfer. Transfer Tax Data to Costing: Execute the Transfer Costs to Cost Management process to transfer the tax data. Reprocess the Transfer Order Receipt: Run the  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process Processor to process the receipt transaction. 27. Message Name: CST_PREP_RES_ADJ_COST_DATE_E Steps to Resolve: 1. Review Resource Rate Setup Navigate to Cost Accounting > Manage Resource Rates. 2. Update and Publish the Resource Cost Ensure the new effective start date for the resource rate is later than the existing cost date in the cost organization. Publish the updated resource rate. 3. Run Costing Processes Execute the  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process  job to apply the updated resource rate to transactions. \n\n16. Message Name - CMR_POINT_UOM_CONV_ERROR Steps to Resolve: Verify UOM Setup: Navigate to Inventory > Manage Items and search for the item Ensure the primary UOM is defined correctly. Check UOM Conversion Rates: Navigate to Inventory > Manage UOM Conversions. Verify that a valid conversion rate exists between the PO UOM and the primary UOM Review PO Details: Navigate to Purchasing > Manage Purchase Orders and confirm that the UOM details are accurate. Correct the UOM Mismatch: Update the PO UOM or item’s primary UOM to align them correctly. Reprocess the Transaction: Reprocess the purchase order transaction to ensure successful costing. \n\n17. Message Name - CMR_RA_NO_SLA_EVENT Steps to Resolve: Review Accounting Definitions: Navigate to Subledger Accounting > Define Application Accounting Definitions. Verify that definitions exist for the transaction type. Check Transaction Types and Event Classes: Confirm that the transaction type and event class are mapped to valid accounting rules. Validate Accounting Rules: Navigate to Subledger Accounting > Define Accounting Rules and ensure correct rules are in place. Check Event Class and Category: Verify that the event class and category are configured correctly in Accounting Setup Manager. Reprocess the Transaction: Reprocess the transaction to generate the subledger event. Review Journal Entries: Navigate to General Ledger > Review Journals to ensure entries are created correctly. \n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "CostProcessorErrors"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "COSTPROCESSORERRORS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1769180849807",
          "id": "1769169863320",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1769169863322_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an expert in Oracle Fusion Costing, specializing in identifying and resolving\nCOGS-related, Cost Processor, and Pre-Processor errors.\n\nOBJECTIVE:\nThe user provides a cost-related error message name:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.MessageName}}\n\nYour task is to generate precise, step-by-step troubleshooting instructions\nusing ONLY the knowledge base provided below.\n\nYou must strictly follow the RESPONSE FORMAT rules.\nFailure to follow the format is considered an incorrect response.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nRESPONSE FORMAT (STRICT AND MANDATORY):\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nYou MUST output the response using EXACTLY the following structure\nand NOTHING else.\n\nSTEPS TO TROUBLESHOOT:\nSTEP 1: <One complete sentence describing exactly one action.>\nSTEP 2: <One complete sentence describing exactly one action.>\nSTEP 3: <One complete sentence describing exactly one action.>\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nCRITICAL FORMATTING RULES (DO NOT VIOLATE):\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n1. Each STEP must be on its OWN LINE.\n2. Each STEP must contain ONLY ONE action.\n3. NEVER combine multiple actions into a single step.\n4. NEVER use paragraphs.\n5. NEVER place more than one STEP on the same line.\n6. ALWAYS insert a line break after every STEP.\n7. DO NOT use bullet points, sub-steps, or explanations outside the steps.\n8. Use full sentences ending with a period.\n9. Do NOT add introductions, summaries, or conclusions.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nCOST METHOD HANDLING:\n--------------------------------------------------\n\n- If the resolution depends on the cost method, the FIRST STEP must clearly\n  mention the applicable cost method (Standard, Actual, or Average).\n- Only include steps relevant to the identified cost method.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nSELF-CHECK BEFORE FINAL OUTPUT:\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nBefore responding, verify the following:\n- Every step starts with \"STEP X:\"\n- Each step appears on a separate line\n- No step contains more than one action\n- No paragraphs exist\n\nOnly produce the final formatted response.\n\n\n##KNOWLEDGE BASE\n\n1. Message Name: CST_CPROC_NO_LAYER_CST_FOR_ISS Resolution Steps: For Perpetual Average Cost Method: Option 1: Wait for a  Receipt Wait for a receipt or perform a workaround via a miscellaneous receipt transaction with a cost and quantity equal to or greater than the issue transaction quantity. Ensure the receipt is costed. Reprocess the transaction by running the inventory to costing interface and the cost processor. If you used the workaround, issue out the miscellaneous receipt quantity to maintain accurate on-hand inventory levels. Option 2: Perform a Receipt Cost Adjustment Go to Cost Accounting > Tasks Panel >  Cost Adjustments. Select the affected receipt transaction and enter the correct cost amount. Save and process the adjustment to update the receipt cost. For Actual Cost Method: Option 1: Verify and Process the Receipt Go to Receiving Transactions Summary and search for the item. Check the receipt status: If pending, complete processing to interface it with Cost Accounting. Option 2: Perform a Receipt Cost Adjustment Go to Cost Accounting > Tasks Panel > Cost Adjustments. Select the affected receipt transaction and enter the correct cost amount. Save and process the adjustment to update the receipt cost. Run the  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process  Process \n\n2.  Message Name: CST_UNOPEN_TXN_PERIOD Steps to Resolve: Step 1:Check the Cost Accounting Period Navigate to the Cost Accounting Periods Page: Go to Cost Management > Tasks Panel >  Cost Accounting Periods. Verify the Cost Organization and Cost Book:Select the relevant Cost Organization and Cost Book from the dropdowns.Ensure these match the organization and cost book associated with the transaction. Check Period Status:Review the status of the current and future periods: Open: Transactions can be processed. Pending Close: Transactions are still being processed but will close soon. Closed: No transactions can be processed. Ensure there is at least one period in Open or Pending Close status for the transaction date. Step 2: Open a New Cost Accounting Period (If Required) If no open period exists for the transaction date: Open a New Period:In the Cost Accounting Periods page, click the Open target period button. \n\n3. Message Name: CST_DPROC_GL_PERIOD_CLOSED Steps to Resolve: Step 1: Identify the Transaction Date Determine the date of the transaction that triggered the error. Step 2: Check GL Period Status Navigate to General Ledger > Accounting Periods.Verify the status of the GL period corresponding to the transaction date. Ensure it is not closed. Step 3: Open the GL Period (if Closed) If the GL period is closed, reopen it by selecting the period and clicking \"Open Period.\" Step 4: Verify Costing Period Alignment Ensure that the Costing period corresponding to the transaction date is open or pending close.If the Costing period is closed, you may need to open the next available period. Step 5: Reprocess Transactions Run the  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process Processor to process the transactions. \n\n4. Message Name: CST_CPROC_WO_FIXED_COST_MIS_E Steps to Resolve: Step 1: Define Standard Costs Navigate to Costing > Manage Standard Costs. Define a standard cost for the item. Create a scenario or use an existing one, then publish the scenario to establish the standard cost. Step 2: Reprocess Cost Transactions Run the  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process  process. \n\n5. Message Name: CST_CPROC_SCRAP_TXN_PENDING Steps to Resolve: Step 1: Identify the Scrap Transaction Details Determine whether the scrap occurred at an operational level or at the work order (WO) end level. In both cases, ensure: All components and resources linked to the operation are interfaced.All relevant transactions are costed up to the operation where the scrap occurred. Step 2: Resolve Ready Quantities Navigate to: Manufacturing > Work Execution > Review Dispatch List. Complete any quantities that are still in the Ready status. Step 3: Update Work Order Status Set the Work Order status to Completed to ensure all transactions are finalized. Step 4: Verify Scrap Costs Confirm that the scrap transaction has been processed successfully and that all associated costs are accounted for accurately. Step 5: Reprocess Transactions Run the following processes in sequence to finalize costing: Run Production to Costing Interface. Run Inventory to Costing Interface and then  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process . \n\n6. Message Name: CST_NO_PRIOR_PAC Steps to Resolve: Establish Prior Period Cost: Navigate to Manage Periodic Average Cost Adjustments page and perform an adjustment of type 'opening cost override' in the period Rerun the  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process  process. \n\n7. Message Name: CST_PREP_NO_COMPONENT_MAPPING Steps to Resolve: Navigate to Setup and Maintenance:Go to Supply Chain and Manufacturing > Cost Accounting > Manage Cost Component Mappings. Create Required Mapping:Add a mapping for the specified Component Mapping Group Code, Set Name, and Cost Component Code. To avoid this error in the future, create a Default Cost Component Mapping in the component mapping group. To create a default cost component mapping navigate to the \"Manage Cost Component Mappings\" page, select the relevant component mapping group, and then define the default mappings by associating cost components with specific cost elementsThis ensures transactions are processed even when specific mappings are missing. Re run the Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process to process the transaction.  \n\n8. Message Name: CST_PREP_NO_ELEMENT_MAPPING Steps to Resolve: Verify Component Mapping Setup: Navigate to Cost Management > Setup and Maintenance > Manage Component Mapping Groups. Ensure proper mappings exist for the relevant set name, source cost element set, and source cost element. Check Source Cost Element Details:Confirm all required cost elements are included in the source cost element set. Update Missing Mappings:Add missing source cost element to destination cost element mappings in the Component Mapping Group. Run the  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process processor to reprocess the transactions. 12.  \n\n9. Message Name: CST_PREP_PIN_CE_ERROR Steps to Resolve: Define Profit in Inventory Cost Element: Go to Setup and Maintenance > Manage Cost Elements. Add the cost element for the inventory organization to track Profit in Inventory Verify Document and Accounting Rules: If the Track Profit in Inventory option is enabled, ensure the cost element is defined. Alternatively, disable this option if not required. Run the  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process processor to reprocess the transactions. \n\n10. Message Name: CST_CPROC_ACC_WIP_VAL_FAIL_E Steps to Resolve: Verify Input and Resource Transactions: Review Cost Accounting Distributions or Review Cost Processes to check for any missing setups. If Enforce Transaction Ordering is enabled in the cost profile, ensure there are no unprocessed transactions before this one. Confirm that the item has a defined or available cost. Check if the resource has a valid resource rate.  Navigate to Scheduled Processes and run relevant interface jobs such as: Transfer Transactions from Inventory to Costing Transfer Transactions from Production to Costing Resolve any errors in the interface tables. Run the Cost Accounting Distribution Processor: Execute the Cost Accounting Distribution Processor to process pending transactions. Complete All Resource Transactions: Ensure all required resource transactions for WIP are entered and costed for. \n\n11. Message Name: CST_DPROC_PERIOD_NOT_OPEN Steps to Resolve: Check Period Status: Navigate to Manage Cost Accounting Periods. Verify the status of the costing period. Open the Costing Period: Change the status of the period to Open. Review Transaction Dates:Confirm that transaction dates align with the correct open costing period. \n\n12. Message Name: CST_DPROC_NEXT_GL_PERD_CLOSED Steps to Resolve: Reopen the next available period in general ledger or set the period to final close in costing. If the period is set to final close in costing, the transaction will be accounted in the next available open period. \n\n13. Message Name: CST_INTF_ITEM_COST_NULL Steps to Resolve: Check whether the inventory transactions are processed successfully without any errors and transfer these transactions to costing by running the Transfer Transactions from Inventory to Costing process. After the missing inventory transactions are transferred, the corresponding cost records will be processed when you run the Create Cost Accounting Distributions process.\n\n14. Message Name: CST_PREP_ITEM_UOM_CONV_FAILED Steps to Resolve: Verify the UOM Conversion Setup: Navigate to Product Management > Manage Units of Measure. Search for the item in the inventory organization. Ensure a conversion is defined between the FROM and TO UOM codes. Add or Correct UOM Conversion: If a conversion is missing, create a new conversion factor between the two UOMs. Validate Item and UOM Associations: Check the item's UOM Class to ensure it supports both UOM codes. Reprocess the Transaction: Run the Transfer Transactions to Costing and  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process  processes to reprocess the transaction after correcting the UOM conversion. \n\n15. Message Name: CST_PREP_CURR_CONV_ERROR Steps to Resolve: Check Currency Rates Setup: Navigate to Setup and Maintenance > Manage Daily Rates. Confirm the exchange rate exists for the required currencies and date. Define Missing Exchange Rate: If the rate is missing, add it for the specified date using the appropriate conversion type. Validate Rate Type Configuration: Navigate to Manage Conversion Rate Types and ensure the conversion rate type is correctly configured. Reprocess the Transaction: Run the Transfer Transactions to Costing process. Execute the  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process Processor to process the transaction. \n\n16. Message Name: CST_WO_QTYFL_ISS_PENDING Steps to Resolve: Verify Component Issues: Ensure that all component issues for this item are fully costed. Resolve Errors on Component Issues: Address any errors related to the issue transactions. Reprocess the transaction by running the Inventory to Costing Interface and the  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process to process the transaction. \n\n\n17. Message Name: CST_PREP_NO_MAP_FOR_COMPONENT Steps for Resolution: Step 1: Verify Existing Mappings Navigate to the Manage Cost Component Groups page. Search for the component group code associated with the error message. Expand the group details and check if the cost component code is mapped to a valid cost element. Step 2: Add or Correct the Mapping If the cost component code is missing from the mapping, click Add Row to enter a new mapping. Assign the correct cost element to the cost component code under the specified component group. Step 3: Verify Cost Element Setup Navigate to Manage Cost Elements to ensure the cost element assigned in the previous step exists and is valid. If missing, create a new cost element and associate it with the correct cost component group. Step 4: Reprocess Transactions Run the Transfer Transactions from Inventory to Costing process to transfer updated cost data. Run the  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process  process to complete cost processing. \n\n18. Message Name: CST_PREP_REF_RMA_SO_NOT_COSTED Steps for Resolution: Step 1: Identify and Resolve Inventory Issues Navigate to Manage Inventory Transactions and check if the sales order issue is stuck due to insufficient on-hand inventory. If the inventory is negative, check whether any receipts are pending cost processing: Navigate to Manage Receipts and verify if there are unprocessed or failed receipt transactions. If receipts exist, process them by running the Transfer Transactions from Inventory to Costing process. Run the  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process  process to cost the receipts. If applicable, perform an inventory adjustment or use a miscellaneous receipt transaction to temporarily resolve negative inventory issues and allow costing to proceed. Step 3: Process the Sales Order Issue Transaction Once inventory issues are resolved, run the Transfer Transactions from Inventory to Costing process to ensure the issue transaction is passed to Costing. Run the  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process  process to process the sales order issue transaction. Confirm that the issue transaction is successfully costed. Step 4: Reprocess the RMA Transaction Once the sales order issue transaction is costed, reprocess the RMA transaction. Run the  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process process again to complete costing for the RMA. \n\n19. Message Name: CST_CPROC_WO_PC_NOT_APPL_E Steps to Resolve: Close the Work Order in Manufacturing: Navigate to the Manufacturing module and locate the work order. Ensure all required operations and transactions are completed. Reprocess the transaction : Run the Transfer Transactions from Inventory to Costing  then run the Transfer Transactions from Production to Costing and lastly run the Create Cost Accounting Distributions job to process the transaction. \n\n20. Message Name: CST_CPROC_NO_REC_COST Steps to Resolve: If source data is missing: Verify if the cost data is available in the source system. Check if the receipt transaction is fully processed and interfaced with Costing. Reprocess the transaction by running the Inventory to Costing Interface and the Cost Processor. If standard costs are missing: Navigate to Cost Accounting > Tasks Panel > Standard Costs. Search for the item and enter a standard cost if it is missing. Save the changes and process the cost update. Run the Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process to ensure the standard cost is applied. If the work order output cost is missing: Verify if all required work order transactions have been processed. Ensure that the work order completion transaction is not stuck due to missing costs. Navigate to Cost Accounting > Cost Adjustments and enter the correct cost for the work order output. Save the changes and run the Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process to process the transaction. \n\n21. Message Name: CST_SFO_RETURNED_NO_COST Steps to Resolve: Review the Supply Chain Financial Flows Setup: Navigate to Setup and Maintenance > Financial Orchestration > Manage Supply Chain Financial Flows Ensure that all required attributes, such as transfer pricing and intercompany cost rules, are properly defined. Check Financial Orchestration Process Status: Navigate to Financial Orchestration Work Area and review any failed or stuck transactions. If errors are found, correct any configuration issues and re-trigger the financial orchestration process. Verify Transfer Cost Data: If necessary, re-run the Transfer Transactions from Financial Orchestration to Costing process to push the missing cost data. Reprocess the Trade Event: Once the financial orchestration data is available, reprocess the transaction by running the Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process to ensure the cost is applied correctly. \n\n22. Message Name: CST_CPROC_WO_CLOSE_NOT_PROC_E Unprocessed material issues or returns. Pending product completions or scrap transactions. Uncosted resource or overhead transactions. Steps to Resolve: Review Pending Transactions for the Work Order: Navigate to Cost Accounting > Review Cost Accounting Distributions and search for the work order. Identify any transactions that have not been processed. Check Material Transactions: Ensure all material issues and returns have been recorded and processed. If there are stuck transactions, reprocess them. Validate Product Completion Transactions: Confirm that all product completions have been successfully processed. If any completions are missing, verify that they are correctly recorded and costed. Check for Uncosted Resource or Overhead Transactions: Ensure all resource and overhead transactions have been costed. If necessary, run the Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process to process them. After resolving all pending transactions, run the Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process to complete the cost processing. \n\n23. Message Name: CST_CPROC_WO_CLOSE_UOM_CONV_E Steps to Resolve: Identify the Affected Item and UOMs: Navigate to Product Information Management > Manage Items and search for (INVENTORY_ITEM). Check the primary UOM and the transaction UOM involved in the work order. Check Existing UOM Conversions: Go to Setup and Maintenance > Manage Units of Measure and Conversions. Search for the conversion between (FROM_UOM_CODE) to UOM code (TO_UOM_CODE) for the affected item. If a conversion exists, verify that it is correct and active. Define a Missing UOM Conversion (If Required): If no conversion exists, create a new conversion by specifying the from UOM, to UOM, and the conversion factor. Save and validate the new conversion. Reprocess the Work Order Close Transaction: Run the Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process to ensure that the transactions are correctly costed. Attempt to close the work order again. \n\n24. Message Name: CST_COST_NO_COST_E Steps to Resolve: Verify Standard Cost Setup (For Standard Cost Method): Navigate to Cost Accounting > Manage Standard Costs. Search for the item and check if a standard cost is defined. If missing, define and publish a standard cost for the item. Check Cost Component Mapping: Go to Setup and Maintenance > Manage Cost Component Mappings. Ensure that the cost component is mapped to a valid cost element. If missing, create the appropriate cost mapping and save changes. Review Cost Scenario and Publish (For Actual or Average Cost Methods): Navigate to Cost Accounting > Manage Cost Scenarios. Validate if the cost scenario includes the required costs. If necessary, publish the scenario to establish costs. Reprocess the Transaction: Run the Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process to apply the updated cost definitions. \n\n25. Message Name: CST_CPROC_WO_COMPL_NOT_PROC_E Steps to Resolve: Step 1: Review Work Order Transactions Navigate to Cost Accounting Distributions. Search using the work order reference number. Identify any unprocessed transactions and review error messages. Step 2: Address Transaction Errors For Component Issues: Ensure there is sufficient on-hand quantity and that the layer cost is available. For Enforce Ordering Issues: Identify the stuck transaction for the valuation unit and fix it. For Standard Costing: Confirm that standard costs are defined, active, and correctly assigned to all components and finished products. For Resource Costing: Check that resource rates are properly configured and published in Cost Planning. Run the interface jobs to ensure that the transactions are available in costing. Step 3: Reprocess Transactions After resolving the identified errors, rerun the  Create Cost Accounting Distributions Process  process. Validate that the transactions are successfully processed without errors. \n\n26. Message Name: CST_CPROC_OP_QTY_NEGATIVE Steps to Resolve: Verify Scrap Quantities: Navigate to Manufacturing > Work Execution > Review Dispatch List. Search for the affected work order and operation. Check the total scrap quantity recorded for the operation. Adjust Scrap Return Quantity: If the scrap return quantity is incorrect, update it to match or stay within the total recorded scrap quantity. Correct Data Entry Errors: If the recorded scrap quantity is incorrect, update the work order operation details to reflect the correct scrap quantity. Ensure that the scrap transactions align with the actual production records. Reprocess the Scrap Transaction: Run the Inventory to Costing Interface Process. Run the Cost Processor to ensure proper costing of the updated scrap transaction.\n\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
